<title>SLOVENIA: Slovenia foreign tourists up 14 pct in 1996.</title>
<headline>Slovenia foreign tourists up 14 pct in 1996.</headline>
<dateline>LJUBLJANA 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The number of foreign tourists in Slovenia rose 14 percent in 1996 to 831,426, the Tourist Association at the Slovenian Chamber of Economy said on Monday.</p>
<p>Foreigners represented 50.2 percent of the tourists in Slovenia last year. The number of domestic guests eased by two percent to 825,005.</p>
<p>The association said revenue was expected to rise to $1.2 billion from $1.1 billion in 1995.</p>
<p>-- Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-125-8439</p>
